 61CO    26MG(48CA,2A4NPG):XUNDL-2     2015AY02                           201505
 61CO c  Compiled (unevaluated) dataset from 2015Ay02:                          
 61CO2c  Phys Rev C 91, 044327 (2015)                                           
 61CO c  Compiled by J. Chen (NSCL, MSU), May 4, 2015                           
 61CO c  Edited by B. Singh (McMaster), May 7, 2015                             
 61CO c  Multinucleon transfer in inverse kinematics                            
 61CO c  2015Ay02: E=275, 290 and 320 MeV {+48}Ca beams were produced from the  
 61CO2c  Argonne Tandem Linear Accelerator System (ALTAS). Target was a         
 61CO3c  self-supporting 0.973 mg/cm{+2} {+26}Mg. |g rays were detected with the
 61CO4c  Gammasphere 4|p array of 101 Compton-suppressed HPGe detectors         
 61CO5c  surrounding the target and reaction residues were  analyzed with the   
 61CO6c  Fragment Mass Analyzer (FMA) and identified on event-by-event basis    
 61CO7c  from the position and time-of-flight measured in a microchannel plate  
 61CO8c  detector (MCP) placed at the focal plane and the energy loss measured  
 61CO9c  with a threefold segmented ionization chamber positioned behind the    
 61COac  focal plane. Measured E|g, I|g, |g|g-coin, |g(|q), |g|g(|q),           
 61CObc  Doppler-shift attenuation. Deduced levels, J, |p, bands, |g-ray        
 61COcc  multipolarities, quadrupole moment. Comparisons with shell-model       
 61COdc  calculations.                                                          
 61CO cG $Angular correlation ratio is defined as:                              
 61CO2cG R{-ac}=I|g(|q=forward/backword)/I|g(|q=90|'), with R{-ac}>1.0 for      
 61CO3cG stretched-quadrupole and <0.8 for stretched-dipole transitions         
 61CO4cG (2015Ay02).                                                            
 61CO cG RI$Compilers' note: several intensitis are quoted with unrealistic     
 61CO2cG uncertainties of 0.3% or less. It is possible that the quoted          
 61CO3cG uncertainties are statistical only.                                    
 61CO cG M$As given in 2015Ay02 based on measured |g(|q) and |g|g(|q) data.     
 61CO2cG Compilers' note: for several |DJ=1, M1+E2 transitions, negative A{-4}  
 61CO3cG values are given, but expected values should be positive for all       
 61CO4cG mixing ratios (see for example graphs in 1975Ta04: NIM 123, 73; and    
 61CO5cG tables in ADNDT 13, 407 (1974))                                        
 61CO cG M(X)$|DJ=0 transition                                                  
 61CO cL E$From a least-squares fit to |g-ray energies (by compilers). The      
 61CO2cL 959.1-, 1150.9- and 2076.3-keV |g rays fit poorly in the level scheme, 
 61CO3cL these were omitted for the fitting purpose, with a resultant reduced   
 61CO4cL |h{+2}=2.1. Without this adjustment, reduced |h{+2}=4.9.               
 61CO cL J$As given in 2015Ay02 based on measured |g-ray angular distributions  
 61CO2cL and correlations and band structures.                                  
 61CO CL BAND(A)$Dipole band 1                                                  
 61CO CL BAND(B)$Yrast dipole band 2.                                           
 61CO2cL Possible magnetic-dipole rotational (shears) band                      
 61CO CL BAND(C)$Dipole band 3                                                  
 61CO CL BAND(D)$Dipole band 4                                                  
 61CO CL BAND(E)$Quadrupole band 1.                                             
 61CO2cL With measured transition Q=1.9 {I+8-11} using                          
 61CO3cL the Doppler-shift attenuation method (DSAM), corresponding to          
 61CO4cL a quadrupole deformation of |b{-2}=0.4 {I2} (2015Ay02).                
 61CO CL BAND(F)$Quadrupole band 2                                              
